    "gmcm.bonus-mult.name": "Weekly goal JP multiplier",
    "gmcm.bonus-mult.tooltip": "How much extra Junimo Points a donation earns when it fills one of this week's theme goals.",
    "gmcm.starting-money.name": "Starting gold each loop",
    "gmcm.starting-money.tooltip": "Gold you begin every loop with, before any Seed Money upgrades.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.section": "Difficulty",
    "gmcm.difficulty.blurb": "Pick a level here to set every option below at once. You can still change any of them one at a time. Everything starts on Normal, the balance the mod ships with. Changes take effect on your next loop.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.overall.name": "Difficulty",
    "gmcm.difficulty.overall.tooltip": "Sets every difficulty option below to this level. You can still change any of them after.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.step.easy": "Easy",
    "gmcm.difficulty.step.normal": "Normal",
    "gmcm.difficulty.step.hard": "Hard",
    "gmcm.difficulty.step.extreme": "Extreme",
    "gmcm.difficulty.stack-size.name": "Stack size",
    "gmcm.difficulty.stack-size.tooltip": "How many of an item a bundle slot asks for, as a share of what a week of going after it actually yields: Easy 10-30%, Normal 20-50%, Hard 50-65%, Extreme 65-80%, never above 80%. Fish, forage, crops, crab pots, monster drops, the mines, animals and machines each have their own yield, and a yield is capped at one stack of 99 (Slime, Bat Wings and the like), so an Extreme ask of 80 is a stack, not a share. One-offs like books and artifacts stay at one. Money bundles are never affected. Works on TLY Custom and on vanilla boards.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.once-per-loop.name": "Once-per-loop items ask for one",
    "gmcm.difficulty.once-per-loop.tooltip": "Some items a loop can only give once: the five legendary fish, the two books hidden around town (The Alleyway Buffet, Mapping Cave Systems) and the Golden Pumpkin from the Spirit's Eve maze. On, a bundle never asks for more than one of them, whatever Stack size says. Off, they scale like everything else, and a Hard or Extreme board can ask for two of something you can only get once. Takes effect at the next reset; a board already asking for two is lowered on load while this is on.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.quality-asks.name": "Quality asks",
    "gmcm.difficulty.quality-asks.tooltip": "How often a slot wants a silver or gold star, which means fertiliser, skill levels and better fishing. Items the game never gives a star to are still never asked for at quality, at any step. Works on TLY Custom and on vanilla boards.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.required-slots.name": "Required slots",
    "gmcm.difficulty.required-slots.tooltip": "How many of a bundle's shown items you must actually donate. Hard asks for one more, Easy one fewer, Extreme asks for all of them. This is the dial that adds real work rather than moving it around. Works on TLY Custom and on vanilla boards.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.item-rarity.name": "Item rarity (TLY Custom only)",
    "gmcm.difficulty.item-rarity.tooltip": "Weights bundles toward harder items: rarer, later in the year, or needing a keg or a press. This one does nothing on vanilla Standard or Remixed boards, because changing which item a vanilla bundle asks for would be changing the bundle.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.jp-earned.name": "Junimo Points earned",
    "gmcm.difficulty.jp-earned.tooltip": "Scales every JP award: donations, bundle and room completions, the weekly quest, season checkpoints and vault payments. Lower means slower progress across loops. The season ramp keeps its shape, so late-season donating is still worth the most.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.shrine-prices.name": "Upgrade prices",
    "gmcm.difficulty.shrine-prices.tooltip": "Scales what upgrades cost in the upgrade menu. Same points, less to show for them.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.starting-gold.name": "Starting gold",
    "gmcm.difficulty.starting-gold.tooltip": "Scales the Starting money value above, rather than replacing it, so a hand-tuned amount is still honoured. Extreme starts you with nothing at all.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.cart-slots.name": "Starting cart slots",
    "gmcm.difficulty.cart-slots.tooltip": "How many items the Traveling Cart offers before you buy any Cart Stall upgrade. On Hard and Extreme the cart is EMPTY until you buy Cart Stall I. Does nothing if the Traveling Cart limit is turned off.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.hold-prices.name": "Hold prices",
    "gmcm.difficulty.darkness.name": "Darkness",
    "gmcm.difficulty.darkness.tooltip": "How hard the darkness hits from Summer on. Sets how many crops or stored items a blight night takes, and whether the darkness checks that you can still get an item back before it undoes a donation or changes what a bundle asks for. Easy and Normal only take what you can replace in time. Hard and Extreme can take anything once a loop, and on Extreme a blight night can also reach tools and machines. The three switches under Features still turn each front off.",
    "gmcm.difficulty.hold-prices.tooltip": "Scales the JP price of keeping your bundle board on a Fail night. The first hold stays free at every step: this makes repeat holds expensive, it does not tax your first mistake.",

    "intro.skip-notice": "Skip intro is on. The Longest Year opens with the story of how you came to the valley and what the Junimos need from you. Watch it the first time you play. Turn Skip intro off to see it.",

    // -- the expanded opening (deathbed, letter, arrival event) ------------------
    "opening.grandpa-1-m": "...and for my very special grandson:",
    "opening.grandpa-1-f": "...and for my very special granddaughter:",
    "opening.grandpa-2": "I want you to have this sealed envelope.",
    "opening.grandpa-3": "No, no. Don't open it yet. Have patience.",
    "opening.grandpa-4": "Now, listen close.",
    "opening.grandpa-5": "There will come a day when you feel crushed by the weight of your life.",
    "opening.grandpa-6": "An emptiness will grow in you and take the light out of you. I know it well. I fought it most of my life.",
    "opening.grandpa-7-m": "When that happens, my boy, you'll be ready for this gift.",
    "opening.grandpa-7-f": "When that happens, my dear, you'll be ready for this gift.",
    "opening.grandpa-8": "Now, let Grandpa rest.",
    "opening.letter-m": "Dear {0},^^If you're reading this, you must be in dire need of a change.^^The same thing happened to me, long ago. I'd lost sight of what mattered most in life... real connections with other people and nature. So I dropped everything and moved to the place I truly belong.^^^I've enclosed the deed to that place... my pride and joy: {1} Farm. It's located in Stardew Valley, on the southern coast. It's the perfect place to start your new life.^^Lastly, the old community center meant a great deal to me. I tried to restore it, but I wasn't strong enough. But I think you are...^^This was my most precious gift of all, and now it's yours. I know you'll honor the family name, my boy. Good luck.^^Love, Grandpa^^P.S. If Lewis is still alive say hi to the old guy for me, will ya?",
    "opening.letter-f": "Dear {0},^^If you're reading this, you must be in dire need of a change.^^The same thing happened to me, long ago. I'd lost sight of what mattered most in life... real connections with other people and nature. So I dropped everything and moved to the place I truly belong.^^^I've enclosed the deed to that place... my pride and joy: {1} Farm. It's located in Stardew Valley, on the southern coast. It's the perfect place to start your new life.^^Lastly, the old community center meant a great deal to me. I tried to restore it, but I wasn't strong enough. But I think you are...^^This was my most precious gift of all, and now it's yours. I know you'll honor the family name, my dear. Good luck.^^Love, Grandpa^^P.S. If Lewis is still alive say hi to the old guy for me, will ya?",
    "event.opening.robin-1": "Hello! You must be @. I'm Robin, the local carpenter. Mayor Lewis sent me to bring you up to the farm.",
    "event.opening.robin-2": "I knew your grandfather. Everyone loved him, and he helped a bunch of individuals become a community. It hasn't been the same since he passed.",
    "event.opening.robin-3": "Up at the farm, as it happens. You can follow us.",
    "event.opening.morris-bus-1": "Excuse me. Morris, Joja Corporation. Where would I find the mayor?",
    "event.opening.robin-walk-1": "This is %farm farm. It's overgrown, but the soil is good.",
    "event.opening.robin-walk-2": "And here we are, your new home.",
    "event.opening.lewis-1": "Welcome, @! I'm Lewis, Mayor of Pelican Town. Everyone's been asking about you.",
    "event.opening.morris-farm-1": "Mayor Lewis. Morris, Joja Corporation. I'll be brief.",
    "event.opening.morris-farm-2": "The Community Center is a registered historical landmark, but because it has been left to rot, our petition to turn it into a Joja warehouse has been approved.",
    "event.opening.morris-farm-3": "I've been assigned to manage the local JojaMart and see the contract through. You'll find me there.",
    "event.opening.lewis-2": "Wait, it says here if we restore it to working condition before Spring 1 of next year this contract is automatically voided.",
    "event.opening.morris-farm-4": "That isn't much of a concern. We've done our research and know there's no money for it in the town budget.",
    "event.opening.morris-farm-5": "@, I recognize you. Why would you leave Joja for... this? Once you grow tired of this game come see me at the store, I could use a company man as my assistant.",
    "event.opening.lewis-3": "The Community Center? Sure. Come on, I'll walk you over. It's not much to look at anymore.",
    "event.opening.lewis-hall-1": "Here it is. We used to have such wonderful times here together. Now it's a mess, and nobody has the time or the money to fix it.",
    "event.opening.lewis-hall-2": "Here, take the key. Look around if you like since it won't be here much longer. Good luck with the farm, @.",
    "event.opening.junimo-1": "Hello, @. We are the Junimos, the spirits of this land.#$b#Few people can see us anymore.$h",
    "event.opening.junimo-2": "Long ago the people of this valley worked the land together and shared what it gave them.#$b#This hall was the heart of that.$h",
    "event.opening.junimo-3": "Then they grew busy. They chased money and forgot one another.#$b#The hall went quiet, and we went to sleep.$s",
    "event.opening.junimo-4": "We can make the land strong again, but not alone.#$b#Work the soil. Bring the town back together.#$b#As they share the land's bounty again, our power returns and this hall is restored.$h",
    "event.opening.junimo-5": "But the seasons bind you, @. Each one asks its share.#$b#Bring enough to this hall before a season turns.#$b#Fall short, and the year unwinds to spring and you begin again.$s",
    "event.opening.junimo-6": "Even at a good pace, one year is too short.#$b#You will not finish on this first turning.#$b#When the year unwinds, everything returns: the fields, the buildings, even the people you have come to know. What you gathered is lost.$s",
    "event.opening.junimo-7": "But what you have learned need not be lost.#$b#Your offerings become our power, and we will spend it to help you keep some of what you gained.#$b#Some of what a season asks may look out of reach. Gather what you can and keep the rest for later.$h",
    "event.opening.junimo-8": "We will turn the year as many times as it takes. There is no shame in beginning again.#$b#Now go home, @. We will meet you there.$h",
    "event.opening.tour-1": "We have given you several gifts that will help make sure each rewind doesn't destroy all that you have built.",
    "event.opening.tour-2": "This is your stash. What you put in it survives the rewind. It holds four things for now. With your help we can make it bigger.",
    "event.opening.tour-3": "This statue will show you what boons we are able to grant you. Some last forever, others are only temporary.",
    "event.opening.tour-4": "This is your cookbook. Write a recipe in it and you keep it through the rewind.",
    "event.opening.tour-5": "This is your craft book. It works the same way, for the things you build.",
    "event.opening.tour-6": "This is your bundle log. It shows every bundle and what each one still needs this season. Check it frequently.",
    "event.opening.tour-7": "One more thing. Each week you can choose a focus, which will give us extra power when you donate certain things of that type.",
    "event.opening.tour-8": "We will also make it easier to find those things, however other types may become harder until you bring all that we ask.",
    "event.opening.tour-9": "Now we begin. Choose wisely, @.",

    // -- year one ending: the crack (spec 2026-09-06 section 6) -----------------------
    "event.ending.crack.open": "Something is going on here that I don't understand.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1": "You've only been here a year, but I remember you giving me a present at least two different times.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2": "I can remember {{scene}}, but how many times did that happen?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3": "The very first time I saw you, I could have sworn we'd already met.",
    "event.ending.crack.close": "I don't know how. But I want to help.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1.Shane": "You've been here a year. So how come I remember you giving me a present at least twice?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2.Shane": "I remember {{scene}}. So how come I remember it more than once?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3.Shane": "The first time I saw you, I could've sworn I already knew you. Figured it was the beer.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1.George": "A year, you say. Then why do I remember you giving me presents two different times? Hmph.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2.George": "I remember {{scene}}. So why do I remember it twice, if you've only been here a year?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3.George": "First time I laid eyes on you, I could've sworn we'd met. And my memory isn't that bad.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1.Haley": "You've only been here a year, right? Because I totally remember you giving me a present at least two different times.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2.Haley": "I totally remember {{scene}}. But how many times did that even happen?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3.Haley": "The very first time I saw you, I thought I already knew you. Weird, right?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1.Abigail": "You've only been here a year, but I remember you giving me a present at least two different times. That's so weird.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2.Abigail": "I remember {{scene}}. But I swear it happened more than once. Weird.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3.Abigail": "The very first time I saw you, I could have sworn we'd already met. Isn't that weird?",
    "event.ending.crack.tier1.Wizard": "You have been here one year. Yet I recall gifts from your hand on two occasions. Curious.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier2.Wizard": "I recall {{scene}}. Yet it seems to have happened twice. Curious.",
    "event.ending.crack.tier3.Wizard": "The first time I saw you, I was certain we had met before. Curious.",
    "event.ending.scene.abigail-2": "playing that video game with you",
    "event.ending.scene.alex-2": "throwing the gridball around on the beach with you",
    "event.ending.scene.elliott-2": "showing you around my cabin",
    "event.ending.scene.emily-2": "that dream we both had",
    "event.ending.scene.haley-2": "you walking in on Emily and me fighting",
    "event.ending.scene.harvey-2": "your check-up at the clinic",
    "event.ending.scene.leah-2": "showing you my sculpture",
    "event.ending.scene.maru-2": "testing soil samples with you",
    "event.ending.scene.penny-2": "you helping me with George's wheelchair",
    "event.ending.scene.sam-2": "you sitting in on our band practice",
    "event.ending.scene.sebastian-4": "showing you my bike up on the mountain",
    "event.ending.scene.shane-2": "that beer we had outside the ranch",

    // -- year one ending: the six-scene script (spec 2026-09-06 section 4) -------------
    "event.ending.lewis-porch-1": "@! There you are. Come quick.$h",
    "event.ending.lewis-porch-2": "The Community Center is lit up. The whole town is out there. Come on!",
    "event.ending.lewis-hall-1": "Everyone. I can't explain what happened here overnight.#$b#But this building is ours again.",
    "event.ending.lewis-hall-2": "We may not have said it, but we all saw you working in here this past year.",
    "event.ending.lewis-hall-3": "The Community Center belongs to Pelican Town again. Thank you.",
    "event.ending.morris-1": "Congratulations. I respect a competitor who can deliver.",
    "event.ending.morris-2": "Joja will be closing its Pelican Town store, effective today.",
    "event.ending.morris-3": "Our survey crews found enough iridium in the Skull Cavern to fund a resort on Ginger Island.",
    "event.ending.morris-4": "This location was barely worth the paperwork to begin with, so we'll focus on mining for now.",
    "event.ending.morris-5": "Don't worry, we'll bounce back from this in no time. We're too big to fail.",
    "event.ending.junimo-1": "You did it, @. The hall is whole, and so are we.",
    "event.ending.junimo-2": "We sang all night.",
    "event.ending.junimo-3": "Did you see the Joja man? The Darkness has him so strongly we can see its hold on him.",
    "event.ending.junimo-4": "Though the people still don't see, they're beginning to sense something. Your bonds give us a foothold with them.",
    "event.ending.junimo-5": "When the new year dawns, our work begins anew.",
    "event.ending.grandpa": "Child, you've started what I couldn't finish. I'm so proud, but you must keep going.",
    "event.turn.summer-1": "Thank you @. You've done well. But something dark has noticed our work here.",
    "event.turn.summer-2": "We have enough power to hold it back thanks to your gifts, but some attacks may slip through our guard.",
    "event.turn.summer-3": "Prepare yourself, we know you can do this.",
    "event.turn.summer-3-again": "Prepare yourself. We have taken much from you. We must take more, but know that it will end.",
    "event.turn.fall-1": "You have been working hard. We are growing stronger.",
    "event.turn.fall-2": "It grows stronger as well. As the days grow shorter, it will reach further.",
    "event.turn.fall-3": "You must continue. We will hold back what we can, but the work is yours alone.",
    "event.turn.winter-1": "This is the last season, @. If it is to end, it ends here.",
    "event.turn.winter-2": "The agents of the enemy will not stop, but with the cold and dark of Winter, it may attack directly.",
    "event.turn.winter-3": "It will corrupt whatever it can. To go on, you must mend what it breaks.",
    "event.turn.winter-4": "If you win here, this cycle will be broken. But I fear our war will continue.",
    "event.darkness.tamper-1": "@, every {{old}} is tainted now.",
    "event.darkness.tamper-2": "The darkness has touched them. We can no longer use them for our restoration.",
    "event.darkness.tamper-3": "Bring us {{new}} instead. It remains pure.",

    // -- day-28 cutscene (preserve @, #$b#, $h) ----------------------------------------
    "cutscene.day28.continue": "Great job, @, you're doing well!#$b#Keep this up and we'll save the valley together. We'll gain even more power from the work you do this season.$h",

    // -- rewind bedroom scene (RewindBedroomScene; Jeff's text, verbatim) --------------------
    "cutscene.rewind.junimo-1": "@, you have worked hard, but we have not gained enough power to proceed.",
    "cutscene.rewind.junimo-2": "Your efforts have attracted the attention of our adversary. It is coming for you now, and we cannot hold it back.",
    "cutscene.rewind.junimo-3": "But the work must continue, we cannot fail here. So we will use what power we have to give you another chance.",
    "cutscene.rewind.junimo-4": "The year will begin again, and the darkness will sleep once more, until the light begins to grow.",
    "cutscene.rewind.morning": "We have bought you more time. Use it and what remains of our power wisely, and remember that every step you take is a small victory.",

    // -- deja-vu villager dialogue (spec 2026-08-27; lines approved by Jeff) ----------------
    // Keys dejavu.<npc lower-case>.<tier>.<n>; the "default" pool covers any villager without lines.
    "gmcm.dejavu.name": "Deja-vu dialogue",
    "gmcm.dejavu.tooltip": "Villagers you have spent a lot of time with across loops occasionally half-remember you. Rare, no gameplay effect. Off = never.",
    "gmcm.blight.name": "Darkness: blight",
    "gmcm.blight.tooltip": "From Summer, some nights a few crops are struck down and a few things in your chests spoil or go missing. The Junimo Stash is never touched. The shrine sells wards against it. Off: nothing is struck or taken.",
    "gmcm.reversion.name": "Darkness: donations come undone",
    "gmcm.reversion.tooltip": "From Fall, about once a week a donated item vanishes from an unfinished bundle. No ward stops this. Off: donations always stay.",
    "gmcm.tampering.name": "Darkness: the board changes",
    "gmcm.tampering.tooltip": "In Winter, up to twice, an unfilled bundle slot switches to a different item. No ward stops this. Off: the board never changes.",
    "dejavu.default.1.1": "Have we met before? You seem familiar.",
    "dejavu.default.1.2": "I swear we've met before. Do you have a twin?",
    "dejavu.default.1.3": "Sorry, I swear I knew your name for a second.",
    "dejavu.default.2.1": "I don't know why, but I feel very comfortable with you.",
    "dejavu.default.2.2": "You feel like an old friend. Isn't that strange?",
    "dejavu.default.2.3": "I feel like I can trust you. I couldn't say why.",
    "dejavu.abigail.1.1": "Weird question. Have we hung out before? Like, before you moved here?",
    "dejavu.abigail.2.1": "I feel like I could tell you anything. I don't even know why.",
    "dejavu.alex.1.1": "You look like someone I used to toss the gridball around with. Can't place it.",
    "dejavu.alex.2.1": "You're easy to be around. Not everyone is.",
    "dejavu.caroline.1.1": "I keep thinking I've already had you over for tea. I'm sure I haven't.",
    "dejavu.caroline.2.1": "You feel like an old friend to me. Isn't that odd?",
    "dejavu.clint.1.1": "Did you bring me an ore sample before? No. I don't know who that was.",
    "dejavu.clint.2.1": "I'm not good with people. But you're all right.",
    "dejavu.demetrius.1.1": "I keep having a sense of recognition when I see you. No data to support it.",
    "dejavu.demetrius.2.1": "I shouldn't feel this comfortable around someone I've known so briefly. Yet here we are.",
    "dejavu.dwarf.1.1": "You familiar. Dwarf remember faces. Dwarf not remember yours.",
    "dejavu.dwarf.2.1": "You friend. Old friend. Dwarf not know why old.",
    "dejavu.elliott.1.1": "Forgive me, but have we met in another chapter? You seem like a character I've written before.",
    "dejavu.elliott.2.1": "I feel I have known you for years, not months. Pleasant, whatever the cause.",
    "dejavu.emily.1.1": "Your aura feels familiar. That's a strange thing to say out loud.",
    "dejavu.emily.2.1": "The universe keeps putting you in my path. I don't mind.",
    "dejavu.evelyn.1.1": "Oh, dear. For a moment I thought you were someone I knew a long time ago.",
    "dejavu.evelyn.2.1": "You feel like family, dear. I couldn't tell you why.",
    "dejavu.george.1.1": "Hmph. You again. Feels like you've been bothering me for years.",
    "dejavu.george.2.1": "You're all right. Don't let it go to your head.",
    "dejavu.gus.1.1": "Funny, I almost poured your usual. You've barely been in.",
    "dejavu.gus.2.1": "You're a regular in here, friend. Longer than I can explain.",
    "dejavu.haley.1.1": "Wait. Have I already told you this? I feel like I already told you this.",
    "dejavu.haley.2.1": "This is going to sound weird, but I feel like I've known you forever.",
    "dejavu.harvey.1.1": "Strange. I keep thinking I've reviewed your chart before. I'm sure I haven't.",
    "dejavu.harvey.2.1": "I feel at ease around you. That's rare for me.",
    "dejavu.jas.1.1": "Have you visited before? A long time ago? You look like someone from a dream.",
    "dejavu.jas.2.1": "You're my friend. I just know it.",
    "dejavu.jodi.1.1": "I thought I'd cooked for you before. Isn't that silly?",
    "dejavu.jodi.2.1": "You're like part of the family already. I'm not sure how that happened.",
    "dejavu.kent.1.1": "You have a way of standing that I recognize. Can't say from where.",
    "dejavu.kent.2.1": "I don't let my guard down with many people. I don't know why you're one of them.",
    "dejavu.krobus.1.1": "Curious. I sense you have walked these tunnels many times. Yet we have only just met.",
    "dejavu.krobus.2.1": "You are comfortable. Like an old stone in the wall.",
    "dejavu.leah.1.1": "I swear I've sketched your face before. Maybe in a dream.",
    "dejavu.leah.2.1": "Being around you feels like sitting by the river. Easy.",
    "dejavu.leo.1.1": "The parrots act like they know you. Did you visit the island before?",
    "dejavu.leo.2.1": "Being with you feels like the island. Safe.",
    "dejavu.lewis.1.1": "You know, for a moment I thought you'd been in the valley for years.",
    "dejavu.lewis.2.1": "I trust you the way I trust folks I've known for decades. Strange, that.",
    "dejavu.linus.1.1": "The wind knows you. I can tell.",
    "dejavu.linus.2.1": "You feel like an old friend. The land seems to think so too.",
    "dejavu.marnie.1.1": "I was about to ask about your animals, but I haven't sold you any, have I?",
    "dejavu.marnie.2.1": "You're always welcome here, dear. Feels like you always have been.",
    "dejavu.maru.1.1": "I keep getting deja vu around you. I should log that.",
    "dejavu.maru.2.1": "I feel like we've already solved a dozen problems together. Maybe we will.",
    "dejavu.pam.1.1": "You look like someone who owes me a drink. Don't know why.",
    "dejavu.pam.2.1": "You're all right, kid. Feels like I've been saying that for years.",
    "dejavu.penny.1.1": "Did I lend you a book once? I could have sworn I did.",
    "dejavu.penny.2.1": "I feel safe talking to you. I don't say that about many people.",
    "dejavu.pierre.1.1": "Have you shopped here before? I feel like I've rung you up a hundred times.",
    "dejavu.pierre.2.1": "You're my best customer. Have been for, hm. How long, exactly?",
    "dejavu.robin.1.1": "Funny. I keep thinking I've built something for you already.",
    "dejavu.robin.2.1": "You feel like an old friend. Don't ask me how.",
    "dejavu.sam.1.1": "Dude, deja vu. Did we already have this exact conversation?",
    "dejavu.sam.2.1": "You're basically one of us at this point. Feels like you always were.",
    "dejavu.sandy.1.1": "Hon, you've got a familiar face. Been out to the desert before?",
    "dejavu.sandy.2.1": "You're a regular in my heart, sugar. Don't know when that happened.",
    "dejavu.sebastian.1.1": "Have we talked before? Like, really talked? Never mind.",
    "dejavu.sebastian.2.1": "I don't usually get comfortable around people. You're the exception, I guess.",
    "dejavu.shane.1.1": "Feels like you've been bugging me for years.",
    "dejavu.shane.2.1": "You're okay. I guess I've felt that way for a while. Don't know why.",
    "dejavu.vincent.1.1": "You look like the person from my dream! Do you have a twin?",
    "dejavu.vincent.2.1": "You're my friend. You always were!",
    "dejavu.willy.1.1": "Ye've got the look of an old deckhand o' mine. Can't be, though.",
    "dejavu.willy.2.1": "I trust ye like I've known ye for years, friend.",
    "dejavu.wizard.1.1": "Curious. Your aura carries echoes. Have we met elsewhere?",
    "dejavu.wizard.2.1": "I sense an old bond between us. Older than it should be."
}
